<title>UK: ADT jumps on Western Resources bid.</title>
<headline>ADT jumps on Western Resources bid.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in ADT Plc soared 100p to 13.12-1/2 stg by 1320 GMT after U.S. group Western Resources said it had launched an offer for ADT, valuing the electronic security systems supplier at $3.5 billion.</p>
<p>Western Resources, which currently holds a 27 percent stake in ADT, said it was making the appeal directly to ADT shareholders.</p>
<p>The bid follows Republic Industries Inc.'s failed $5 billion bid to take over ADT in September.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
